  "sentence": "Four rate-distortion panels side by side, one per video: bear, camel, dog and pigs. Each plots foreground PSNR in decibels against bitrate in kilobits per second over four fixed-QP rungs, with a grey line for the pristine SVT-AV1 baseline and a dashed blue line for the bridge arm. A bridge curve lying left of the baseline delivers the same foreground quality for fewer bits. On bear and camel it does; on dog and pigs it lies to the right instead, and the two curves converge at the most starved rung rather than separating."
